body:
I'm new here. Just want to share observations made when attempting to understand the standard behavior for this case. Tested at [MDN Playground](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/play) using the below code.

HTML:
```HTML
<canvas></canvas>
```

JS:
```JavaScript
let canvas = document.querySelector("canvas");
canvas.style.backgroundColor = "lightgray";

let ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
ctx.lineWidth = Math.min(canvas.width, canvas.height)/2;
ctx.lineCap = "square";
ctx.moveTo(canvas.width/2, canvas.height/2);

ctx.lineTo(canvas.width/2, canvas.height/2);
// (and/or)
// ctx.closePath();

ctx.stroke();
```

<br>

Three cases: `lineTo`, `closePath`, both

Three possibilities: nothing, square (axis-aligned), diamond (45° rotated square)

- Safari: nothing, nothing, nothing. (version 18.6)
- Firefox: square, nothing, nothing! (version 144)
- Chrome: square, square, nothing!! (version 141.0.7390.108)
- CoreGraphics: diamond, diamond, diamond.
